On Tue, Nov 30, 2010 at 11:01:00PM -0800, Robin Lee Powell wrote:
> On Wed, Dec 01, 2010 at 02:37:29PM +1100, Ross Ogilvie wrote:
> > Hey,
> > 
> > I was looking at the BPFK pages today and I noticed that it was
> > treating things in braces as plugins, then throwing errors when
> > it couldn't find those plugins.
> > 
> > Example
> > http://www.lojban.org/tiki/tiki-index.php?page=BPFK+Community+Work
> > {broda} => Internal Error: Plugin *broda* does not exist.
> > 
> > I bring it up because the Community Work page advises people to
> > "Please put {...} around any cross-references to other Lojban
> > words .... This will not get marked up, but it will save us a
> > lot of trouble later."
> 
> Oooooooh.
> 
> The update must have trashed the local fix to turn words into
> jbovlaste links.  *That's* unfortunate.

I was wrong about that, actually.  The updates *did* trash the local
hack, but that hack was to make things like "{jvs klama}" turn into
jbovlaste links.

The real issue was that someone updated trunk (the "in development"
branch) to accept basically *everything* wrapped in {...} as a
plugin.  We've moved to the more stable 6.x branch.  Problem solved.

-Robin

